<% content_for :title, "Important Announcement" %>
<% content_for :page_heading, "Important Announcement (3/21/2020)" %>
<% content_for :page_heading_class, "ptfgRed" %>

<div class="row">
  <div class="col-md-8 ptfgPageWidth">
    <p>
      <b>To: All <%= CurrentSeason.year %> PTFG Participants</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      All canceled tournaments will be getting removed from each league's schedule until play is scheduled to start
      again.  Any golfers selected for a cancelled tournament will be cleared and eligible for usage in a future
      tournament.  For all private leagues playing multiple segments, I will work with your league commissioner(s) to
      re-adjust the segments as per their desire.  But that will not happen until we know when the PGA Tour will start
      playing again. For now, all canceled tournaments will be removed, which means you won't get bothered with any
      system generated set lineup reminder emails, etc.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hard to know what's ahead in these unprecedented times.  I thought the PGA Tour might be the one sport to escape
      the coronavirus pandemic (without a gallery, of course) and help us maintain some source of normalcy, what
      little that might be.
    </p>
    <p>
      As <b>Mark Wetzstein</b>. a commissioner from one of my PTFG private leagues said, much more eloquently than I
      ever could:  <i>"Sports provide us all with an escape and maybe a little joy from time to time. With the whole
      world shutting down, it’s going to be doubly hard to get through the near future without our favorite
      diversions. But the games will come back, and so will we, and when that day comes, I look forward to welcoming
      you all back to <b>Pro Tour Fantasy Golf</b></i>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until then, please stay safe (and healthy).<br><br>
      Regards,<br><br>
      John Hohlen<br>
      <b>Pro Tour Fantasy Golf Founder</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>P.S.</b> Unless you're a commissioner of a private league. please don't email me unless it's about something
      I  haven't answered or something that is still unclear.  I am a one-man show and don't have the capacity to reply
      to a flood of emails.  I take great pride in trying to respond to everyone in a timely fashion (i.e. within 24
      hours) and certainly won't be able to do that under these conditions.  I'm sure most of you have many of the
      same questions and hopefully they have been answered above.  I greatly appreciate everyone's patience.
      understanding, and continued support. This is something I never, ever anticipated when I challenged myself to
      develop the best fantasy golf game on the Internet 15 years ago.  In that time, I believe there have only been
      two tournaments ever canceled and they were both due to weather (2016 Greenbrier Classic in West Virginia and
      the 2009 Viking Classic in Mississippi).
    </p>
  </div>
  <%= render "layouts/right_logo" %>
</div>
